git init => initialize a new git dir
git add => add files to the stage area
git commit -m "<message>" => add staged changes to the commited area
git status => to see working area (tracked, untracked) , staged
git log => see commited area ( your latest commits)
.gitignore => files added here are not tracked by git 


git log --name-only => see changed files
git log --oneline => see a commit in a line commithash + message
git log -n <#> => display only specific number of logs


git branch => see branch and checked branch 
git branch <nameofthebranch> => create new branch
git switch <nameofthebranch> || git checkout <nameofthebranch> => siwth to that branch
git checkout <nameofthebranch> => create a new branch and switch to it
git log <branchname> => see the log of a specific branch